  "style": {
    "id": "uv-reveal",
    "name": "UV Reveal",
    "description": "Two-layer surface revealed by a moving ultraviolet torch: an ordinary printed page (illustration + dummy text) lies on a warm oak desk under bright room light and shows no trace of anything else. A hand-held UV torch switches on, the room light dims, and inside the torch's violet pool a hidden fluorescent layer glows — a repeating watermark lattice, neon contours, a code strip and a big stamp — in saturated cyan, green and magenta on deep violet paper. The pool position, its radius (torch height and beam zoom) and a short phosphor afterglow behind the moving pool are pure functions of t along a planned torch path (torchplan.js); in the shader the visible print sinks to deep violet and the hidden layer is added to the page's emission only where the pool or afterglow masks are non-zero. Final move: the room goes dark, the torch lifts away, the pool radius grows past the sheet and the whole hidden layer glows at once. Switch click, lamp hum, sweep whooshes, per-mark pings and the flood chime come from the same plan.",
